    "b-10-purpose-and-boundary-prompt-kit-is-a-library-2": {
      "id": "b-10-purpose-and-boundary-prompt-kit-is-a-library-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The Prompt Kit library owns typed, composable prompt documents. The workspace adds a filesystem authoring server and external MCP adapter, while Agent Kernel retains model execution, runtime tool registration, sessions, and traces."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-purpose-and-boundary-divider-3": {
      "id": "b-10-purpose-and-boundary-divider-3",
      "type": "divider",
      "props": {},
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-purpose-and-boundary-problem-4": {
      "id": "b-10-purpose-and-boundary-problem-4",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Problem"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-purpose-and-boundary-agent-prompts-need-to-be-5": {
      "id": "b-10-purpose-and-boundary-agent-prompts-need-to-be-5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Agent prompts need to be both human-readable and machine-manipulable. A plain\nMarkdown prompt is easy to read, but hard to validate, transform, substitute, or\npreview consistently. A rigid schema is easy to validate, but can become too\nconstraining for real prompt-writing work."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-purpose-and-boundary-prompt-kit-sits-between-6": {
      "id": "b-10-purpose-and-boundary-prompt-kit-sits-between-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Prompt-kit sits between those poles. Prompts are authored as structured\ndocuments, in code, as JSON documents, or through the editor UI, and\nconsumers can render them to linear text, inspect the tree, replace pieces,\nvalidate integrity, and drive editing surfaces from the same object. The\nmechanics of that object and its operations live in\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "System Design",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "10-system-design/00-overview"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-purpose-and-boundary-package-boundary-7": {
      "id": "b-10-purpose-and-boundary-package-boundary-7",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Package Boundary"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-purpose-and-boundary-prompt-kit-owns-generic-8": {
      "id": "b-10-purpose-and-boundary-prompt-kit-owns-generic-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Prompt-kit owns generic prompt structure: the canonical prompt document, its\nnode vocabulary, rendering to model-facing text, transformation and\ncomposition, validation, and the UI for viewing and editing prompt documents."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-purpose-and-boundary-prompt-kit-does-not-own-9": {
      "id": "b-10-purpose-and-boundary-prompt-kit-does-not-own-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Prompt-kit does not own runtime behavior:"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-purpose-and-boundary-agent-registry-discovery-10": {
      "id": "b-10-purpose-and-boundary-agent-registry-discovery-10",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "agent registry discovery, model selection, or turn limits"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
